 "story": "Calm, both hands resting on her bump, her thumb stroking it. Something's not right — a small intake, her fingers press in, she swallows and her eyes drop. The nausea rises: her far hand leaves her bump and comes up to cover her mouth as her eyes close; she swallows hard behind her hand, then takes one deep breath in — shoulders and ribcage rising — and lets it out slowly, her shoulders dropping. It passes: her hand eases off her lips and comes down to hold her bump, and with both hands on it she softens, looking down at it with love.",
